+// (slab method). The earliest contact wins — a fast ball breaks the FIRST
+// brick it crosses instead of tunnelling through it (defect D2) — and every
+// brick whose expanded box contains the contact point is broken in the same
+// pass, so a seam straddle (gap 8 < ball diameter 14) breaks both bricks with
+// exactly ONE velocity flip per axis (defect D4).
